# RUN: midenc -Zlint -Canalyze-only %S/../../fixtures/masm/cross_module_advice_taint/miden-project.toml 2>&1 | filecheck %s
#
# The lint stops the build by returning `CompilerStopped`, which `midenc-driver` downcasts
# into a *clean* exit. On a project the error now travels back out through the assembler's
# call stack before the driver sees it, so a wrapper introduced anywhere along that path
# would turn this run into a failed compilation. The pipe above cannot catch that -- the
# status observed there is filecheck's -- so assert midenc's own status separately. lit
# joins RUN lines with `&&`, so a non-zero exit here fails the test. Output is left
# unredirected on purpose: if this ever does fail, the error is what you want to read.
# RUN: midenc -Zlint -Canalyze-only %S/../../fixtures/masm/cross_module_advice_taint/miden-project.toml

CHECK-LABEL: lib/support.masm
CHECK:  unconstrained advice data is consumed here as a constrained value

CHECK-LABEL: lib/mod.masm
CHECK: exec.support::dirty
CHECK: unconstrained value is passed as a call argument here

CHECK-LABEL: lib/mod.masm
CHECK: adv_push
CHECK: advice data is obtained here which is later used unconstrained
